(1) Subject to sub-paragraphs (2) and (3), the margin requirements set out in this Joint Standard do not apply to non-centrally cleared OTC derivative transactions entered into between a provider and a counterparty or foreign counterparty in the same group.

(2) Intra-group transactions are not subject to margin requirements provided that—
(a) the aggregate outstanding gross notional amount of the non-centrally cleared OTC derivative transactions between the provider and the counterparty or foreign counterparty in the group is below R100 billion at close of business on each relevant day;
(b) both parties are subject to appropriate centralised risk evaluation, measurement and control procedures;
(c) the risk management procedures of both parties are adequately sound, robust and consistent with the level of complexity of the derivative transactions; and
(d) the parties comply with any further conditions as may be specified by the Authorities.

(1) Subject to paragraph 2, a provider must—
(a) calculate and exchange—
(i) initial margin in accordance with paragraph 4; and
(ii) variation margin in accordance with paragraph 5;
(b) have in place sufficiently robust processes, procedures and board-approved policies, to ensure among other things that—
(i) all relevant transactions between the provider and counterparty comply with all relevant requirements in the legal and regulatory frameworks of each relevant jurisdiction;
(ii) all relevant netting agreements are effective under the laws of the relevant jurisdictions, and supported by periodically updated legal opinions;
(iii) all relevant collateral arrangements are effective under the relevant laws and supported by periodically updated legal opinions;
(iv) the provider exchanges initial and variation margin on a bilateral basis or to a third-party custodian;
(v) procyclicality impacts are appropriately mitigated — large discrete calls for additional initial margin due to 'cliff-edge' triggers are discouraged, and margin levels are sufficiently conservative even during periods of low market volatility;
(vi) initial margin is provided and collected by no later than the business day following execution of a non-centrally cleared OTC derivative transaction;
(viii) variation margin — the full amount necessary to fully collateralise the mark-to-market exposure is exchanged; calculated and exchanged on a daily basis for transactions subject to a single legally enforceable netting agreement;
(ix) the provider complies with eligible collateral requirements in paragraph 6.

(2) A provider must have in place rigorous and robust dispute resolution procedures with its relevant counterparties before the onset of any relevant transaction.

(3) All margin transfers may be subject to a minimum transfer amount of which the aggregate or sum of the initial margin and variation margin does not exceed R5 million.
